<title>BRAZIL: Brazil net dollar outflows $395.8 mln June 19.</title>
<headline>Brazil net dollar outflows $395.8 mln June 19.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Preliminary figures for Brazil's commercial and financial foreign exchange contracts showed a $395.8 million deficit on June 19 in the commercial forex market, according to Central Bank.</p>
<p>Dealers said the net dollar outflow was mostly due to the expiration of Eurobonds.</p>
<p>The Central Bank issued the following breakdown:</p>
<p>DOLLAR FLOWS ON JUNE 19</p>
<p>Exports: $289.8 million</p>
<p>Imports: $343 million</p>
<p>Financial buy: $274.9 million</p>
<p>Financial sell: $617.5 million</p>
<p>Net deficit: $395.8 million</p>
<p>JUNE DOLLAR FLOWS UP DATE</p>
<p>Exports: $3.164 billion</p>
<p>Imports: $3.759 billion</p>
<p>Financial buy: $5.567 billion</p>
<p>Financial sell: $5.145 billion</p>
<p>Net deficit: $173 million</p>
<p>Note: Figures rounded off.</p>
<p>((--Alexandre Caverni, Sao Paulo newsroon, 55 11 2485418))</p>
